{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Sprite Particle Rendering.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Sprite Particle Rendering.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"sprite particle rendering sprite particle rendering","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Sprite Particle Rendering.md","fileName":"Sprite Particle Rendering.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Sprite Particle Rendering","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-15 18:17\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Particle and Destruction VFX]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Particle and Destruction VFX","Geometry-Instanced Particle Debris","digitalvisualeffectsandcompositing.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Sprite Particle Rendering.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Sprite Particle Rendering.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"sprite particle rendering sprite particle rendering","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Sprite Particle Rendering.md","fileName":"Sprite Particle Rendering.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Sprite Particle Rendering","heading":"Sprite Particle Rendering","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Instead of rendering heavy volumes for every particle, an image or footage sprite can be attached to each simulated point. The book uses cloud-image sprites on a fountain-like particle path to make rocket exhaust and a spiraling missile trail. Their speed and visual detail make them useful when the camera view preserves the billboard illusion. A camera move that reveals the cards' flatness or an effect whose debris must spin in volume needs [[Geometry-Instanced Particle Debris]] instead.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Particle and Destruction VFX","Geometry-Instanced Particle Debris","digitalvisualeffectsandcompositing.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Sp